VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, you can see I\'m starting with a rough idea I actually have instead of needing to turn it into something polished before I can build. This same way of giving V6 direction also gets really useful when you\'re working with'

[09:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something you\'ve already created. Let\'s say I really like this song, but I want the chorus to have more energy. Instead of starting over, I can describe the change I want and where I want it to happen. Make the chorus more energetic.'

[09:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Add bigger layered vocals and heavier drums, but keep the verses the same. And now we\'ll make it. And let\'s listen to this new version. In your arms, I find my home. With you,'

[10:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m never alone. Oh, let the years come as they will. I\'m'

[10:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'telling V6 what I want changed and actually where I want the change. You can do that with much smaller details, too. So, maybe I love a song, but there\'s only one word that I want to'

[10:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'replace. I can say something like change the word love to light throughout the song. So, let\'s just play the song where it says love. &gt;&gt; And now let\'s play the new version where'

[10:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it\'s replaced it with light. &gt;&gt; It makes that lyric change while keeping the song and its structure intact. So, a tiny edit doesn\'t mean rebuilding'

[11:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything around it. If you\'ve ever had a song that you\'ve loved except for one line, this is extremely useful. Most of what I\'ve shown you so far is happening in simple mode because that\'s where these new multi-input and plain language'

[11:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workflows really change the experience. But V6 and V6 Wild are also available when you\'re creating in advanced mode. If you prefer writing your own lyrics, entering styles directly, using the more'

[11:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'detailed controls, structuring your song yourself, you can keep working that way while using the new models. One other new control that you\'re going to find under more options now is variety. Normal is the default and raising this'

[11:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gives pseudo more freedom to expand on your style input and explore more distinct directions between the two songs that it creates. If you want to stick more closely to the exact style that you entered, you can turn variety'

[11:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'down or off completely. And if you use my taste, those variations will lean more towards your personal taste profile. Now, let\'s get into V6 Wild, which is the exploratory model. And I'

[12:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'don\'t think that the best way to demonstrate this is just to make one song with V6 and one song with V6 Wild. You won\'t be able to hear the difference there. It\'s going to become more clear if we use the same prompt to create'

[12:20] [scene:talk]
