[14:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is what I mean when I say V6 Wild is designed for exploration. With V6,'

[14:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m generally looking for a more reliable interpretation of what I\'ve asked for. With V6 Wild, I\'m looking through a much broader range of possibilities. And I might not choose to keep every song that V6 Wild creates,'

[14:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but maybe one has a strange rhythm that I really love, or another has an unusual vocal performance, and another introduces an instrument or a melody that gives me a completely different'

[14:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'idea for the song. If you were someone that kept going back to some of Sunno\'s older models because you liked the creativity or the personality, this is part of V6 Wild that I think that you\'re going to appreciate the most. And you'

[14:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'don\'t have to pick one model and stay there for the entire process. I could use V6 Wild to find an idea that I wasn\'t expecting and then take that idea back into V6 when I want to develop it with more precision. That\'s probably the'

[15:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'easiest way to think about the difference. V6 for precision, V6 wild for exploration. The last feature I want to point out is max mode. Max mode gives the model more compute before it creates'

[15:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the song. And it can be useful when you\'re asking it to maintain something consistently over a longer creation. For example, if you\'re working on a song with an audio influence like a cover or'

[15:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'using a voice, max mode can help reduce drift, especially on songs longer than 2 minutes. It can also help keep the overall musical style more consistent as the song develops. You don\'t need to'

[15:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'turn this on every time you make a song, but if you\'re working on something longer or more demanding and you\'re noticing the song start to move away from what you wanted, Max mode is worth trying. So, that\'s your first look at'

[16:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sunno V6. The jump in audio quality is a big part of this release, but I think one of the most exciting changes is how much more directly you can tell what you\'re actually trying to accomplish. You can combine several musical'

[16:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'references in one request. Start with an image, video, or a voice memo. Make targeted changes to something you\'ve already created. Or give Sunno several pieces of creative directions at once. Use flagship V6 when you have a clear'

[16:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'target and want more reliable results. Use V6 Wild when you want to explore a wider range of possibilities and see where they take you. And when you\'re using Pseudo for free, you can start'

[16:39] [scene:talk]
